# Generated plugin artifacts are compared byte-for-byte against freshly
# generated output by `npm run plugin:skill:check` (CI runs it on every
# platform, including windows-latest).
#
# The generators emit LF only: a JavaScript template literal normalises any
# CRLF in its source to LF, and the reference files are built from those
# literals. On a checkout that rewrites files to CRLF — git's
# `core.autocrlf=true`, the default on GitHub's windows-latest runners — the
# committed bytes disagree with the generated ones and the check reports drift
# on files nobody edited. Pinning LF here keeps the worktree byte-identical to
# what the generator produces, on every platform.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf`, so this holds however the checkout is
# configured.
resources/plugin-skill/** text eol=lf
resources/plugin-templates/** text eol=lf
resources/plugin-bundled/** text eol=lf
